  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Warm temperatures and breezy winds Sunday \nbefore the next rain chances early next week.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION... High pressure builds over the \nregion Saturday and moves off the coast to our south Sunday. \nBreezy winds out of the southwest will develop between the high \nand the weakened remnants of Isaias as it moves into the Ohio \nvalley Saturday night into Sunday. These winds will help to \nfunnel warmer temperatures (upper 60s to low 70s) into the area \nfor Sunday and Monday, potentially 10-15 degrees above average \nfor this time of year. As the system moves off the southern New \nEngland coast, it could bring a chance of showers for the \nDowneast coast Sunday night into Monday. Rain chances could \ndecrease if the system stays further south, though there is \nstill a good amount of uncertainty at this time. A separate low \npressure develops over the Great Lakes Monday night as a trough \ndeepens behind the departing tropical remnants. This will bring \na chance of rain early to mid next week.",
